<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39327" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pseudŏthyrum</span></b> ,
		i, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψευδόθυρον</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>a backdoor</i>, <i>private entrance</i>, <i>postern-gate</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">palatii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 14, 1, 3</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Oros. 7, 6 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a secret manner</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(nummi) per pseudothyrum revertantur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 2, 20, § 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non janua receptis, sed pseudothyro intromissis
					voluptatibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Red. in Sen. 6, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
